Subject: [PATCH 04772/11362] [outer-loop] Ledger: LLM-as-tool-driver/MCP lever
 BUILT+RUN -> two-game fair-shot ceiling-negative

Updates the 2026-06-28 tool-use/MCP lever row from "AUDITED not-done-before, NOT YET BUILT" to the
empirical result. The probe (scripts/experiments/arc_frontier_tooluse_probe.py) had a frontier driver
(codex/gpt-5.5) drive the existing subsystems via a sandboxed tool loop; induce backend held constant
(local Qwen) so the only variable is codex-driving. On re86 + ft09 (both fair_shot=True, correctly-aimed
directed clicks: 104 + 117), the driver surfaced ZERO first-level-ups and never beat the one-shot
baseline -> ~12% prior realized as a negative on the tested games. Consistent with WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE.
Honest limitations recorded (n=2; weak local induce; identity-fit accuracy caveat). Two adversarial
sub-agent reviews drove harness fixes (nested-args parser; flat-schema click-coord stripping) before
the result was trusted. Captured so the planner does not re-build it as a scored-agent path; the
dev-convenience use (frontier tool-loop to author GameAdapter deltas) remains positive-EV + untested.

